{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "33b50538-7a6c-4528-b960-cca506a6f91b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 9. REQUEST-URI"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e43a6624-a66d-4a87-852c-3139adae18be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Request-URI identifies the resource that the client wants\n",
    "to access or operate on.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET\n",
    "    → HTTP method\n",
    "\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "    → Request-URI / request-target\n",
    "\n",
    "HTTP/1.1\n",
    "    → HTTP version\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "cb292e83-f709-4ff7-9302-a0843a3704b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "1. REQUEST-URI FORMS\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "In older HTTP/1.1 terminology, Request-URI can appear\n",
    "in four different forms:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Request-URI\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- * (asterisk-form)\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- absoluteURI\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- abs_path\n",
    "       |\n",
    "       +---- authority"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "ff78c973-5458-42a9-ac23-512ab9961445",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "2. ASTERISK-FORM (*)\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Syntax:\n",
    "\n",
    "OPTIONS * HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "* → represents the server as a whole.\n",
    "\n",
    "It does NOT refer to one particular resource.\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Give me information about the HTTP options\n",
    "supported by this server.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "So:\n",
    "\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "    → specific resource\n",
    "\n",
    "*\n",
    "    → entire server\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "0c5f1963-04f6-492a-876c-bd2dd51945aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "3. ABSOLUTE-URI\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Syntax:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET http://example.com/posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here the complete URI is present:\n",
    "\n",
    "http://example.com/posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "This form was mainly used when the client communicates\n",
    "with an HTTP proxy.\n",
    "\n",
    "Flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | GET http://example.com/posts/101\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Proxy\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Server\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Normally, when directly communicating with the server,\n",
    "we commonly see the path form instead:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "71a43946-4f48-413b-a1d7-21f0518c1766",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "4. ABS_PATH\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the normal path form used in an HTTP request.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "    → absolute path (abs_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "The path must begin with:\n",
    "\n",
    "/\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /index.html HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /users/25 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /products/10 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "If the original URI has no path:\n",
    "\n",
    "http://example.com\n",
    "\n",
    "the request uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET / HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "/\n",
    "    → represents the root path of the server."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e8945798-0abe-482d-90af-2721e0863669",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "5. AUTHORITY FORM\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "The authority form is used with the CONNECT method.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "CONNECT www.example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "www.example.com:443\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "     authority\n",
    "\n",
    "It contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Hostname + Port\n",
    "\n",
    "www.example.com → hostname\n",
    "443              → port\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "CONNECT is commonly used to establish a tunnel,\n",
    "for example for HTTPS communication through a proxy.\n",
    "\n",
    "Simple idea:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | CONNECT example.com:443\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Proxy\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | establishes tunnel\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "HTTPS Server\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "0e2bf0ed-b9a3-4f9f-8dac-c663058b8a28",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "6. COMPLETE COMPARISON\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "ASTERISK-FORM\n",
    "\n",
    "OPTIONS * HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Represents the server as a whole.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ABSOLUTE-URI\n",
    "\n",
    "GET http://example.com/posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains the complete URI.\n",
    "Commonly associated with proxy requests.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ABS_PATH\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains only the path.\n",
    "Common form for normal HTTP requests.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "AUTHORITY\n",
    "\n",
    "CONNECT example.com:443 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains hostname + port.\n",
    "Used with CONNECT.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "18b4ff52-3884-46d8-ae0e-31d3e03c783f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "7. CONNECTION WITH URL\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose the complete URL is:\n",
    "\n",
    "https://example.com/posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "Break it into:\n",
    "\n",
    "https://\n",
    "    → Scheme\n",
    "\n",
    "example.com\n",
    "    → Host\n",
    "\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "    → Path\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "A normal HTTP request can then look like:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Host: example.com\n",
    "\n",
    "Notice:\n",
    "\n",
    "Complete URL:\n",
    "https://example.com/posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "Request-URI:\n",
    " /posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "Host header:\n",
    " example.com\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "So the server gets:\n",
    "\n",
    "Host + Request-URI\n",
    "       ↓\n",
    "example.com + /posts/101\n",
    "       ↓\n",
    "Requested resource"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "6fe1efc8-449f-48fc-abb8-0661d5776ef0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "8. IMPORTANT POINT\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Do not confuse:\n",
    "\n",
    "URL\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "Complete address/URI such as:\n",
    "https://example.com/posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Request-URI\n",
    "    ↓\n",
    "The URI form used in the HTTP request line,\n",
    "such as:\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Request line:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "    ↑\n",
    "Request-URI / request-target\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "526f6fee-f0ad-4256-8612-873569f53114",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "MEMORY TRICK\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "*              → Whole server\n",
    "absoluteURI    → Full URI\n",
    "abs_path       → Normal /path\n",
    "authority      → host:port for CONNECT\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "SUMMARY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Request-URI tells HTTP which target the request is\n",
    "intended for.\n",
    "\n",
    "Four older HTTP/1.1 forms are:\n",
    "\n",
    "    *             → Server as a whole\n",
    "    absoluteURI   → Complete URI\n",
    "    abs_path      → Normal resource path\n",
    "    authority     → Host + port, used by CONNECT\n",
    "\n",
    "Most normal requests look like:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /posts/101 HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "/posts/101\n",
    "    → Request-URI / request-target"
   ]
  }
 ],
